---
Run a bash command in the working directory and return its combined output.
---

Each call runs in a fresh shell in the working directory — no state persists
between calls, so avoid `cd`; use paths relative to the working directory or
absolute paths. Output over 20k chars is truncated; the full output is saved to
a file whose path is given in the result, so you can read or grep it there.
Use this for terminal work (git, build, test, run) and for searching (grep/rg,
find); prefer the read/edit/write tools for file contents.
